"""Recorded quantization outputs for ``golden_vectors.py``. DATA ONLY.

Every row is one ``(preset, backend, input dtype)`` case. The inputs that
produced them -- seed, shape, dtypes, seeding protocol -- are defined in
``golden_vectors.py`` and are the only thing needed to reproduce a row.

Regenerating is an explicit act, never a reflex. A red golden test means the
quantization output moved; that is the signal this harness exists to produce.
Re-record only once the move is understood and intended, and name in the commit
message which presets and backends changed and why. The regeneration command
(``record`` or ``record-extended``) is in the ``golden_vectors.py`` docstring,
under "Running it".

Columns of ``GOLDEN_VECTOR_TABLE``, whitespace separated:

    key     ``<preset>|<backend>|<input dtype>``
    shape   output shape, ``<rows>x<cols>``          (asserted)
    dtype   output dtype                             (asserted)
    sha256  SHA-256 over the output tensor's raw bytes (asserted)
    min max mean    diagnostics only, never asserted
    n_nan n_inf     diagnostics only, never asserted
"""

